<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 25 July, from 1139 to 1984.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1139 CE <span class="tih-ago">887 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Afonso Henriques wins the Battle of Ourique</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Afonso Henriques defeated an Almoravid army at Ourique and was soon styling himself King of Portugal. The victory became a founding legend of Portuguese independence from León.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique">Battle of Ourique</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1593 CE <span class="tih-ago">433 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry IV of France converts to Catholicism</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Protestant Henry IV abjured his faith at the basilica of Saint-Denis to win acceptance from Catholic France. The words 'Paris is well worth a Mass' are attributed to him, and he entered Paris the next year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1837 CE <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cooke and Wheatstone demonstrate the electric telegraph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William Cooke and Charles Wheatstone sent messages along a telegraph line between Euston and Camden Town in London. Its success led to the first commercial telegraph on the Great Western Railway.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1978 CE <span class="tih-ago">48 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louise Brown, the first 'test-tube baby', is born</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Louise Brown was born in Oldham, the first person conceived by in vitro fertilisation, pioneered by Robert Edwards and Patrick Steptoe. Millions of people have since been born through IVF.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1984 CE <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Svetlana Savitskaya becomes the first woman to walk in space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet cosmonaut Svetlana Savitskaya spent three and a half hours outside the Salyut 7 space station. She tested a hand-held tool for cutting and welding metal in space.</p></div></li></ol>
